    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0536" n="456" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg456"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1398.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Mr. White’s No. 2039, of the 20th ultimo,
                    has been received.</p>
                <p>The public official explanation of the words “for police reasons” in the order
                    expelling the Eisemann brothers from Prussia appears to be what the Messrs.
                    Eisemann desired, and the incident may therefore be considered closed.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
